**Per-channel table row is not asserted**

Failure: the channel table can be removed or mis-rendered and every test still passes, because only the channels object is checked. Add:
```js
test('the channel table row for summary-only findings is rendered', () => {
  assert.match(render(analyze(mixed())), /\| summary \| 1 \| 1 \| 0% \(0\/1\) \| n\/a \| n\/a \|/);
});
```

